      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A sudden death of a 39-year-old man after physical overload is discussed. Morphological investigation revealed myocardial bridge in the left anterior descending artery, transmural postinfarction scar with aneurysm in the anterior apical region of the left ventricle, and acute myocardial inFarction in the same region. It is supposed that recurring myocardial necrosis developed because of systolic compression of the anterior descending artery during physical overload."},
